{"id":27588,"slug":"l-argent","title":"L’argent","year":1983,"country":"France","duration":84,"spine":886,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/27588-l-argent","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/f700b2d43d7829bc795538602dc4120c/Na4b95E94g2wpH1f7iNU4pZj74NWOZ_large.jpg","description":"In his ruthlessly clear-eyed final film, French master Robert Bresson pushed his unique blend of spiritual rumination and formal rigor to a new level of astringency. Transposing a Tolstoy novella to contemporary Paris, L’argent follows a counterfeit bill as it originates as a prop in a schoolboy prank, then circulates like a virus among the corrupt and the virtuous alike before landing with a young truck driver and leading him to incarceration and violence. With brutal economy, Bresson constructs his unforgiving vision of original sin out of starkly perceived details, rooting his characters in a dehumanizing material world that withholds any hope of transcendence.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Robert Bresson","slug":"robert-bresson"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Christian Patey","role":"Yvon","slug":"christian-patey"},{"actor":"Vincent Risterucci","role":"Lucien","slug":"vincent-risterucci"},{"actor":"Caroline Lang","role":"Elise","slug":"caroline-lang"},{"actor":"Sylvie van den Elsen","role":"Gray-haired woman","slug":"sylvie-van-den-elsen"},{"actor":"Michel Briguet","role":"Gray-haired woman’s father","slug":"michel-briguet"},{"actor":"Didier Baussy","role":"Owner of photography store","slug":"didier-baussy"},{"actor":"Marc Ernest Fourneau","role":"Norbert","slug":"marc-ernest-fourneau"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Robert Bresson","slug":"robert-bresson"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Robert Bresson","slug":"robert-bresson"},{"role":"Based on the short story “Faux billet” by","person":"Leo Tolstoy","slug":null},{"role":"Executive produced by","person":"Antoine Gannagé","slug":null},{"role":"Cinematography by","person":"Pasqualino De Santi